# 💻 Java Code

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Q17 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.print("Please enter no: ");
        int n = sc.nextInt();

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {

            // Print leading spaces
            for (int j = 1; j <= n - i - 1; j++) {
                System.out.print(" ");
            }

            char ch = 'A';

            // Turning point
            int breakpoint = (2 * i + 1) / 2;

            // Print characters
            for (int j = 1; j <= (2 * i + 1); j++) {

                System.out.print(ch);

                if (j <= breakpoint) {
                    ch++;
                } else {
                    ch--;
                }
            }

            System.out.println();
        }

        sc.close();
    }
}
```

---

# ⏱️ Time Complexity

```text
O(N²)
```

**Reason:** The outer loop runs `N` times, and for each row the inner loops print spaces and characters proportional to `N`.

---

# 💾 Space Complexity

```text
O(1)
```

Only a few extra variables are used (`i`, `j`, `ch`, and `breakpoint`).

---

Time Complexity: O(N²), because for each of the N rows, up to 2N characters (spaces and letters) may be printed, 
resulting in O(N²) total operations.

Space Complexity: O(1), as only a constant amount of extra space is used for variables like ch and breakpoint.

# 📚 Key Takeaways

- Uses nested loops to build the pyramid.
- Uses characters instead of numbers.
- Number of characters in each row follows the formula **2 × i + 1**.
- Number of leading spaces follows the formula **n - i - 1**.
- The **Breakpoint** acts as the turning point where the alphabet sequence changes from increasing to decreasing.
- The pattern is horizontally symmetric (palindromic).

---

## ⭐ Core Idea

The **Breakpoint** is the heart of this pattern.

- **Before the breakpoint:** Characters increase (`A → B → C → ...`)
- **At the center:** The highest alphabet is printed.
- **After the breakpoint:** Characters decrease (`... → C → B → A`)

This creates the beautiful symmetric alphabet pyramid.
